Package: fancymaps
Title: Publication-Ready Maps for Spatial Model Output
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Camille", "Ross", email = "camille.ross@maine.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1428-2294"))
Description: Draws the maps a spatial modelling pipeline produces, with the
    parts a reader needs to navigate one: land, a stated projection, a scale
    that was chosen rather than defaulted, and optional scale bar, north arrow
    and locator inset. Handles the quantities these models actually emit --
    a skewed positive surface such as predicted density, a bounded probability
    such as posterior occupancy, a diverging quantity with a meaningful zero
    such as an extrapolation score, and the uncertainty that belongs beside any
    of them. A value and its uncertainty are drawn as one paired figure with a
    shared extent and aligned panels, and a series over time as small multiples
    on one shared scale, because panels drawn separately do not compare.
    Accepts the forms model output arrives in: 'sf' polygons, points and lines,
    'terra' rasters, and a plain data frame with coordinate columns, which is
    what remains once geometry has been dropped for modelling. Shares a visual
    identity with 'fancyfx', which plots the same models' effects and
    evaluation.
